sections:

#### prop_section ####
kind: proposition
----
statement: To find two straight lines incommensurable in square which make the sum of the squares on them medial but the rectangle contained by them rational.
----
proof:

Set out two medial straight lines {AB} and {BC}, commensurable in square only, such that the rectangle which they contain is rational and the square on {AB} is greater than the square on {BC} by the square on a straight line incommensurable with {AB}. <div class="just"><a href="/elements/books/bookX/propositions/propX31/">X.31</a> ad fin.</div>

Describe the semicircle {ADB|semiT} on {AB}. Apply a parallelogram to {AB} equal to the square on {BE} and deficient by a square figure, namely the rectangle {AF} by {FB}. Then {AF} is incommensurable in length with {FB}. [!just VI.28; X.18]

<figure class="diagram">
<canvas id="canvas_0" width="360" height="200" tabindex="0"></canvas>
<noscript><img alt="X.34 diagram" src="propX34.gif"/></noscript>
<script type="text/javascript">
    // Joyce's figure: AB with BC produced beyond B, E bisecting BC, F on AB,
    // the semicircle ADB (random face), the triangle ADB (random face, named
    // tri) and the perpendicular FD. Added, all hidden at rest: solid twins
    // AB, AD, DB (initiallyHidden) so AB stands before the semicircle and
    // the joins stroke from A and D; transparent targets AF, FB, BE
    // (;0;0;0); a faceless, strokeless twin of the semicircle (semiT) to
    // carry its highlight, since the filled one would be raised over the
    // triangle (#140) and the circle that owns the name ADB is the whole
    // circle; right-angle markers at F (by construction) and at D (III.31).
    //
    // Draggables (checked against the bundle): A, B (free), C (line slider)
    // — the givens — and F (line slider), which only arrives with "namely
    // the rectangle AF by FB", so it is deferred. E and D are derived and
    // listed per slide.
    var GIVEN = ["A","B","C","AB","BC"];
    var SEMI  = GIVEN.concat(["semi"]);
    var BE    = SEMI.concat(["E","BE"]);
    var APPL  = BE.concat(["F","AF","FB"]);
    var PERP  = APPL.concat(["D","FD","angF"]);
    var ALL   = PERP.concat(["AD","DB","tri"]);
    var RT    = ALL.concat(["angD"]);
    geomlib.init({
        canvasid: "canvas_0",
        background: "35,19,100",
        title: "X.34",
        elements: [
            "A;point;free;40,160",
            "B;point;free;220,160",
            "C;point;lineSlider;A,B,320,160",
            "BC;line;connect;B,C",
            "M;point;midpoint;A,B;0;0",
            "ADB;circle;radius;M,B;0;0;0;0",
            "E;point;midpoint;B,C",
            "F;point;lineSlider;A,B,190,160",
            "FD';line;perpendicular;F,A;0;0;0",
            "DD';line;chord;FD',ADB;0;0;0",
            "D;point;last;DD'",
            "semi;sector;arc;B,D,A;0;0;black;random",
            "tri;polygon;triangle;A,D,B;0;0;black;random",
            "FD;line;connect;F,D",
            // Slide-only twins, highlight targets and markers.
            "AB;line;connect;A,B",
            "AD;line;connect;A,D",
            "DB;line;connect;D,B",
            "AF;line;connect;A,F;0;0;0",
            "FB;line;connect;F,B;0;0;0",
            "BE;line;connect;B,E;0;0;0",
            "semiT;sector;arc;B,D,A;0;0;0;0",
            "angF;sector;angleMarkerRight;F,A,D",
            "angD;sector;angleMarkerRight;D,A,B"
        ],
        initiallyHidden: ["AB","AD","DB"],
        deferDraggables: ["F"],
        aliases: { "BA": "AB", "BF": "FB", "DF": "FD" },
        slides: [
            { text: "“To find two straight lines incommensurable in square",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["AD","DB"],
              justifications: [{ ref: "X.34" }] },
            { text: "which make the sum of the squares on them medial but the rectangle contained by them rational.”",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["AD","DB"] },
            { text: "Set out two medial straight lines {AB} and {BC}, commensurable in square only,",
              visible: GIVEN,
              highlighted: ["AB","BC"] },
            { text: "such that the rectangle which they contain is rational",
              visible: GIVEN,
              highlighted: ["AB","BC"] },
            { text: "and the square on {AB} is greater than the square on {BC}",
              visible: GIVEN,
              highlighted: ["AB","BC"] },
            { text: "by the square on a straight line incommensurable with {AB}.",
              visible: GIVEN,
              highlighted: ["AB"],
              justifications: [{ ref: "X.31 ad fin." }] },
            { text: "Describe the semicircle {ADB|semiT} on {AB}.",
              visible: SEMI,
              highlighted: ["semiT","AB"],
              transition: { animations: [
                  { elem: "semi", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep } ] } },
            { text: "Apply a parallelogram to {AB} equal to the square on {BE}",
              visible: BE,
              highlighted: ["AB","BE"],
              transition: { animations: [
                  { elem: "E", name: geomlib.A.Point.appear } ] } },
            { text: "and deficient by a square figure, namely the rectangle {AF} by {FB}.",
              visible: APPL,
              highlighted: ["AF","FB"],
              transition: { animations: [
                  { elem: "F", name: geomlib.A.Point.appear } ] },
              justifications: [{ claim: "AF·FB = BE²", ref: "VI.28" }] },
            { text: "Then {AF} is incommensurable in length with {FB}.",
              visible: APPL,
              highlighted: ["AF","FB"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "AF, FB incommensurable in length", ref: "X.18" }] },
            { text: "Draw {FD} from {F} at right angles to {AB},",
              visible: PERP,
              highlighted: ["FD","angF"],
              transition: { mode: "cascade", animations: [
                  { elem: "FD",   name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeConnect },
                  { elem: "angF", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep } ] } },
            { text: "and join {AD} and {DB}.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["AD","DB"],
              transition: { mode: "cascade", animations: [
                  { elem: "AD",  name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeConnect },
                  { elem: "DB",  name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeConnect },
                  { elem: "tri", name: geomlib.A.Polygon.outlineAndFill } ] } },
            { text: "Since {AF} is incommensurable in length with {FB},",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["AF","FB"] },
            { text: "therefore the rectangle {BA} by {AF} is also incommensurable with the rectangle {AB} by {BF}.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["AB","AF","FB"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "BA·AF, AB·BF incommensurable", ref: "X.11" }] },
            { text: "But the rectangle {BA} by {AF} equals the square on {AD},",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["AB","AF","AD"] },
            { text: "and the rectangle {AB} by {BF} equals the square on {DB},",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["AB","FB","DB"] },
            { text: "therefore the square on {AD} is also incommensurable with the square on {DB}.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["AD","DB"] },
            { text: "And, since the square on {AB} is medial, therefore the sum of the squares on {AD} and {DB} is also medial.",
              visible: RT,
              highlighted: ["AB","AD","DB","angD"],
              transition: { animations: [
                  { elem: "angD", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep } ] },
              justifications: [{ claim: "the angle in a semicircle is right", ref: "III.31" },
                               { claim: "AD² + DB² = AB²", ref: "I.47" }] },
            { text: "And, since {BC} is double {DF},",
              visible: RT,
              highlighted: ["BC","FD"] },
            { text: "therefore the rectangle {AB} by {BC} is also double the rectangle {AB} by {FD}.",
              visible: RT,
              highlighted: ["AB","BC","FD"] },
            { text: "But the rectangle {AB} by {BC} is rational, therefore the rectangle {AB} by {FD} is also rational.",
              visible: RT,
              highlighted: ["AB","BC","FD"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "AB·FD rational", ref: "X.6" }] },
            { text: "But the rectangle {AB} by {FD} equals the rectangle {AD} by {DB},",
              visible: RT,
              highlighted: ["AB","FD","AD","DB"] },
            { text: "so that the rectangle {AD} by {DB} is also rational.",
              visible: RT,
              highlighted: ["AD","DB"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "AB·FD = AD·DB", ref: "X.32.Lemma" }] },
            { text: "Therefore two straight lines {AD} and {DB} incommensurable in square have been found",
              visible: RT,
              highlighted: ["AD","DB"] },
            { text: "which make the sum of the squares on them medial, but the rectangle contained by them rational.",
              visible: RT,
              highlighted: ["AD","DB"],
              justifications: [{ ref: "Q.E.D." }] }
        ],
        resolveJustification: function(ref) {
            if (ref === "X.34") return "#prop";
            return (window.eucrefs && window.eucrefs[ref]) || null;
        }
    });

    // Per-page citation lookup for the slideshow's resolveJustification.
    // Joyce's "X.32.Lemma" is the lemma published at the head of X.33.
    window.eucrefs = (window.eucrefs || {});
    Object.assign(window.eucrefs, {
        "I.47":         "/elements/books/bookI/propositions/propI47/",
        "III.31":       "/elements/books/bookIII/propositions/propIII31/",
        "VI.28":        "/elements/books/bookVI/propositions/propVI28/",
        "X.6":          "/elements/books/bookX/propositions/propX6/",
        "X.11":         "/elements/books/bookX/propositions/propX11/",
        "X.18":         "/elements/books/bookX/propositions/propX18/",
        "X.31 ad fin.": "/elements/books/bookX/propositions/propX31/",
        "X.32.Lemma":   "/elements/books/bookX/propositions/propX33/#lemma"
    });
</script>
</figure>

Draw {FD} from {F} at right angles to {AB}, and join {AD} and {DB}.

Since {AF} is incommensurable in length with {FB}, therefore the rectangle {BA} by {AF} is also incommensurable with the rectangle {AB} by {BF}. [!just X.11]

But the rectangle {BA} by {AF} equals the square on {AD}, and the rectangle {AB} by {BF} equals the square on {DB}, therefore the square on {AD} is also incommensurable with the square on {DB}.

And, since the square on {AB} is medial, therefore the sum of the squares on {AD} and {DB} is also medial. [!just III.31, I.47]

And, since {BC} is double {DF}, therefore the rectangle {AB} by {BC} is also double the rectangle {AB} by {FD}.

But the rectangle {AB} by {BC} is rational, therefore the rectangle {AB} by {FD} is also rational. [!just X.6]

But the rectangle {AB} by {FD} equals the rectangle {AD} by {DB}, so that the rectangle {AD} by {DB} is also rational. <div class="just"><a href="/elements/books/bookX/propositions/propX32/#lemma">X.32.Lemma</a></div>

Therefore two straight lines {AD} and {DB} incommensurable in square have been found which make the sum of the squares on them medial, but the rectangle contained by them rational.

<div class="qed">Q.E.D.</div>
